For anyone maintaining both files (or using the `@AGENTS.md`-in-CLAUDE.md adapter pattern above), the painful part isn't the one-time setup — it's keeping them from drifting and silently breaking as each gets hand-edited.

I open-sourced a small CLI for exactly that: **[skillcraft](https://github.com/cloudroad-io/skillcraft)** (`pip install skillcraft`, MIT). You author one canonical `AGENTS.md` and it:

- **syncs** `CLAUDE.md` / `SKILL.md` from it — `sync --check` fails CI the instant a target drifts (including target-side edits);
- **lints** all three (kebab-case names, frontmatter, `@import` cycles, token budget, merge markers) — `--format=github` annotates PRs;
- carries richer metadata through `AGENTS.md` via invisible HTML comments, so same-format round-trips are lossless.

It doesn't add AGENTS.md support to Claude Code itself (that's Anthropic's call — +1 the issue), just makes authoring and maintaining these files sane in the meantime. Plugin API is frozen; a few [good-first-issues](https://github.com/cloudroad-io/skillcraft/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22) are open if anyone wants cursor/copilot support next.

I agree with supporting `AGENTS.md`, but I would treat it as a repo-authored operating contract, not just a neutral alias for `CLAUDE.md`.

The useful distinction is:

- `AGENTS.md`: portable repo-level context for any coding agent;
- tool-specific overlays: `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, etc.;
- generated context: summaries, indexes, cached plans, and run traces;
- user/session directives: temporary intent that should not rewrite the repo contract.

That gives teams a clean adoption path: keep stable project rules in `AGENTS.md`, keep Claude-specific behavior in Claude-owned files, and avoid silently merging generated memory back into authored repo context.

One implementation detail I would like to see is an inspectable source order: which instruction files were loaded, from which directory, with what precedence, and whether anything was ignored. That would make multi-agent repos much easier to debug.

I have been exploring this broader structure in a Personal AI OS / memory vault model where authored memory, agent overlays, and generated views are separate layers: https://github.com/hegu-1/personal-ai-os

@bcherny Claude Code should automatically read AGENTS.md if no CLAUDE.md exists. That "solution" in the linked doc still requires including a CLAUDE.md file for Claude Code support. It's a workaround, not actual adoption of AGENTS.md.

You can learn more about the AGENTS.md standard here: https://aaif.io/projects/agents-md (you guys should know this one)

Is there any reason not to do the 2 lines of code change to automatically read AGENTS.md? Would it be because it benefits Anthropic for people to include CLAUDE.md advertisements in their repos?

@Bistard although it is funny, but it is bad idea. CLAUDE.md can still hold Claude specific rules that are tied directly to calude's behavior. Especially glob user-level one.  Inside project repository it is arguably not needed. 

I wuldn't want it to contain vague "This instrction applies only if you are Claude agent"

And my instructions have lot of stuff specific to Claude -- how subagent works, how async tool calling works, quirks of WebFetch etc. All this has zero value for other agents.

@jeremycastanza CC is not opensource. This repo is onlt for Issues (and this issues are mostly ignored).

Some of stuff that I've sent to feedback@anthropic.com got implemented. at least for Claude Deskop.

But I didn't got any reply beyond automated message that my letter is logged.

Merge this into `~/.claude/settings.json`'s toplevel dictionary:

```
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear|compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "f=\"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}/AGENTS.md\"; if [ -f \"$f\" ] && ! [ -f \"${f%AGENTS.md}CLAUDE.md\" ]; then echo '=== AGENTS.md (project rules) ==='; cat \"$f\"; else true; fi",
            "statusMessage": "Loading AGENTS.md..."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
```
